{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Activity: practice with data wrangling in pandas\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "editor: source\n",
        "callout-icon: false\n",
        "ipynb-shell-interactivity: all\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# Wrangling with exam grades\n",
        "\n",
        "You work in the Office of Institutional Research at a large university, and your boss asks you to investigate the relationship between student evaluations and scores on the final exam in introductory statistics courses.\n",
        "\n",
        "We have two CSV files to investigate this question. The `exam_grades.csv` file contains last semester's final exam scores for 800 students taking introductory statistics across 30 different sections. The columns include:\n",
        "\n",
        "* `student_id`: a unique 4-digit identifier for each student\n",
        "* `classid`: which of the 30 sections the student was enrolled in\n",
        "* `professor_name`: the name of the professor which whom the student took the class. Each professor teaches several sections\n",
        "* `exam_score`: the student's score on the final exam. All introductory students take the same final exam, regardless of course section\n",
        "\n",
        "Your boss also provides you with information on each professor's course evaluations. The `professor_evals.csv` file contains evaluations for each of the 10 professors teaching introductory statistics. The `classid_1`, `classid_2`, and `classid_3` columns identify the 3 sections taught by each professor, while the three `evalscore` columns contain the professor's corresponding course evaluation scores (out of 5) for each class.\n",
        "\n",
        "You can import the data with"
      ],
      "id": "af0dc27f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "\n",
        "professor_evals = pd.read_csv(\"https://sta261-f26.github.io/class_activities/professor_evals.csv\")\n",
        "exam_grades = pd.read_csv(\"https://sta261-f26.github.io/class_activities/exam_grades.csv\")"
      ],
      "id": "f748993f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Reshape the `professor_evals` data so it looks like this:"
      ],
      "id": "7e68dffe"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "\n",
        "pivoted_evals = pd.wide_to_long(professor_evals,\n",
        "  stubnames = ['classid', 'evalscore'],\n",
        "  i = 'name',\n",
        "  j = 'class',\n",
        "  sep = \"_\")\n",
        "  \n",
        "pivoted_evals"
      ],
      "id": "c7a9e6f7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:**"
      ],
      "id": "476045d6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pivoted_evals = pd.wide_to_long(professor_evals,\n",
        "  stubnames = ['classid', 'evalscore'],\n",
        "  i = 'name',\n",
        "  j = 'class',\n",
        "  sep = \"_\")\n",
        "  \n",
        "pivoted_evals"
      ],
      "id": "60d98b0b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Using the `exam_grades` data, compute the mean score for each professor and class:"
      ],
      "id": "4d408255"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "mean_scores = exam_grades.groupby(['professor_name', 'classid']).agg(mean_score = ('exam_score', 'mean'))\n",
        "\n",
        "mean_scores"
      ],
      "id": "8ccbf110",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:**"
      ],
      "id": "837c8f32"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "mean_scores = exam_grades.groupby(['professor_name', 'classid']).agg(mean_score = ('exam_score', 'mean'))\n",
        "\n",
        "mean_scores"
      ],
      "id": "86c8644a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Use `merge` to combine the results from the last two questions into a single data frame:"
      ],
      "id": "5063089b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "comb_data = mean_scores.reset_index().merge(pivoted_evals.reset_index(), how='left', left_on = ['professor_name', 'classid'], right_on = ['name', 'classid']).drop(['class', 'name'], axis=1)\n",
        "comb_data"
      ],
      "id": "035b9dc9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "**Note:** to include columns in the final data frame which are indexes in the previous data frames, you may need to reset the index before merging. This can be done with [`reset_index`](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.reset_index.html)\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:**"
      ],
      "id": "c185c12e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "comb_data = (mean_scores.reset_index()\n",
        "  .merge(pivoted_evals.reset_index(), \n",
        "         how='left', left_on = ['professor_name', 'classid'], \n",
        "         right_on = ['name', 'classid'])\n",
        "  .drop(['class', 'name'], axis=1))\n",
        "\n",
        "comb_data"
      ],
      "id": "3a14687e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Plotting\n",
        "\n",
        "After creating the combined data in the previous question, we may want to look at the relationship between mean exam score and course evaluation score. There are a variety of options for creating graphics in Python; one possibility is the `plotly` package. Here is an example:"
      ],
      "id": "aea306a2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import plotly.express as px\n",
        "\n",
        "fig = px.scatter(comb_data, x = 'mean_score', y = 'evalscore',\n",
        "  hover_data = ['professor_name', 'classid'],\n",
        "  labels = {'mean_score': 'Mean exam score', \n",
        "    'evalscore': 'Average course evaluation score',\n",
        "    'professor_name': 'Professor',\n",
        "    'classid': 'Class'},\n",
        "  trendline = 'ols')\n",
        "fig.show()"
      ],
      "id": "609b7536",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# UFC Fights\n",
        "\n",
        "In the second part of this activity, we will work with data on UFC fights and athletes.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question:** How do physical attribute advantages such as height, reach, or age differences correlate with the likelihood of winning a bout?\n",
        "\n",
        "## Data\n",
        "\n",
        "We have two different datasets available: `ufc_athletes.csv` contains information on each fighter, while `ufc_fights.csv` contains information on each fight. These datasets can be loaded into Python with:"
      ],
      "id": "2c2efda0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "ufc_athletes = pd.read_csv('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rfordatascience/tidytuesday/main/data/2026/2026-07-07/ufc_athletes.csv')\n",
        "ufc_fights = pd.read_csv('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rfordatascience/tidytuesday/main/data/2026/2026-07-07/ufc_fights.csv')"
      ],
      "id": "12732ad3",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### `ufc_athletes.csv`\n",
        "\n",
        "|variable              |class     |description                           |\n",
        "|:---------------------|:---------|:-------------------------------------|\n",
        "|name                  |character |Athlete name as listed in the dataset.|\n",
        "|nickname              |character |Athlete nickname, where available. |\n",
        "|weight_class          |character |Athlete's listed UFC weight class. |\n",
        "|url                   |character |URL for the athlete's UFC profile page. |\n",
        "|profile_name          |character |Athlete name as shown on the UFC profile page. |\n",
        "|profile_nickname      |character |Athlete nickname as shown on the UFC profile page, where available. |\n",
        "|status                |character |Athlete status, such as '\"Active\"' or '\"Not Fighting\"'. |\n",
        "|place_of_birth        |character |Athlete's listed place of birth. |\n",
        "|age                   |double    |Athlete age in years, where available. |\n",
        "|height                |double    |Athlete height in inches, where available. |\n",
        "|weight                |double    |Athlete listed weight in pounds, where available. |\n",
        "|octagon_debut         |date      |Date of the athlete's UFC debut, where available. |\n",
        "|sig_strikes_landed    |double    |Total significant strikes landed in UFC competition. |\n",
        "|sig_strikes_attempted |double    |Total significant strikes attempted in UFC competition. |\n",
        "|sig_str_landed        |double    |Significant strikes landed per minute. |\n",
        "|sig_str_absorbed      |double    |Significant strikes absorbed per minute. |\n",
        "|takedown_avg          |double    |Average takedowns landed per 15 minutes. |\n",
        "|submission_avg        |double    |Average submission attempts per 15 minutes. |\n",
        "|sig_str_defense       |double    |Significant strike defense rate, expressed as a proportion. |\n",
        "|takedown_defense      |double    |Takedown defense rate, expressed as a proportion. |\n",
        "|knockdown_avg         |double    |Average knockdowns landed per 15 minutes. |\n",
        "|average_fight_time    |Period    |Athlete's average UFC fight time, where available. |\n",
        "|takedowns_attempted   |double    |Total takedown attempts in UFC competition, where available. |\n",
        "|fighting_style        |character |Athlete's listed fighting style, where available. |\n",
        "|reach                 |double    |Athlete reach in inches, where available. |\n",
        "|leg_reach             |double    |Athlete leg reach in inches, where available. |\n",
        "|takedowns_landed      |double    |Total takedowns landed in UFC competition, where available. |\n",
        "|trains_at             |character |Athlete's listed gym or training affiliation, where available. |\n",
        "|wins                  |character |Athlete's listed career wins. |\n",
        "|losses                |character |Athlete's listed career losses. |\n",
        "|draws                 |character |Athlete's listed career draws. |\n",
        "|standing_count        |double    |Number of significant strikes landed at distance. |\n",
        "|standing_pct          |double    |Proportion of significant strikes landed at distance. |\n",
        "|clinch_count          |double    |Number of significant strikes landed in the clinch. |\n",
        "|clinch_percent        |double    |Proportion of significant strikes landed in the clinch. |\n",
        "|ground_count          |double    |Number of significant strikes landed on the ground. |\n",
        "|ground_percent        |double    |Proportion of significant strikes landed on the ground. |\n",
        "|ko_tko_win            |double    |Number of wins by knockout or technical knockout. |\n",
        "|ko_tko_percent        |double    |Proportion of wins by knockout or technical knockout. |\n",
        "|dec_wins              |double    |Number of wins by decision. |\n",
        "|dec_percent           |double    |Proportion of wins by decision. |\n",
        "|sub_wins              |double    |Number of wins by submission. |\n",
        "|sub_percent           |double    |Proportion of wins by submission. |\n",
        "\n",
        "### `ufc_fights.csv`\n",
        "\n",
        "|variable             |class     |description                           |\n",
        "|:--------------------|:---------|:-------------------------------------|\n",
        "|fight_url            |character |URL for the fight details page on [http://ufcstats.com/](http://ufcstats.com/) |\n",
        "|event_name           |character |Event Name |\n",
        "|date                 |date      |Date of the UFC event. |\n",
        "|location             |character |Event location, usually formatted as city and country or city and state. |\n",
        "|f1_name              |character |Name of the first listed fighter. |\n",
        "|f1_result            |character |Result for the first listed fighter, typically \"W\" for win or \"L\" for loss. Missing for scheduled or incomplete bouts. |\n",
        "|f2_name              |character |Name of the second listed fighter. |\n",
        "|f2_result            |character |Result for the second listed fighter, typically \"W\" for win or \"L\" for loss. Missing for scheduled or incomplete bouts. |\n",
        "|weight_class         |character | Weight class or bout category, such as \"Bantamweight Bout\" or \"Heavyweight Bout\". |\n",
        "|method               |character |Method of victory, such as \"Decision - Unanimous\", \"KO/TKO\", or \"Submission\". Missing for scheduled or incomplete bouts. |\n",
        "|round                |double    |Round in which the fight ended. Missing for scheduled or incomplete bouts. |\n",
        "|time                 |Period    |Time elapsed in the final round when the fight ended. Missing for scheduled or incomplete bouts. |\n",
        "|time_format          |character |Scheduled fight format, such as \"3 Rnd (5-5-5)\" or \"5 Rnd (5-5-5-5-5)\". |\n",
        "|referee              |character |Name of the referee. Missing for scheduled or incomplete bouts. |\n",
        "|judging_details      |character | Judges' score card details; If fight ends with a KO, TKO or Submission, details are provided|\n",
        "\n",
        "## Questions\n",
        "\n",
        "To answer the question, we will need to combine information from the `ufc_fights` and `ufc_athletes` datasets. To combine this information correctly, we need to understand what information uniquely identifies an athlete.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Duplicate athletes?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Does name uniquely identify a row in the `ufc_athletes` data? To help answer this question, the following code identifies all rows in the `ufc_athletes` data with a *duplicated* name:"
      ],
      "id": "c02c7f17"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "ufc_athletes[ufc_athletes.duplicated(['name'], keep = False)]"
      ],
      "id": "9ddffdc2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Look at the other columns in the data. For the individuals with duplicate names, which ones appear to be the *same* person (showing up multiple times) and which appear to be *different* people (who just happen to have the same name)?\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:** It seems like Casey Kenney, Keiichiro Nakamura, and Richie Vaculik are the duplicates (The others just share the same name). \n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Based on your answer to the previous question, can you find a set of columns that uniquely identify each athlete, and which are also available in the `ufc_fights` data?\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:** The combination of name and weight class seem sufficient to identify an athlete.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "We only want to keep one row per athlete in the `ufc_athletes` data. The `drop_duplicates` function will remove rows which have duplicate information in a specified set of columns:"
      ],
      "id": "b2c5c754"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "\n",
        "ufc_athletes = ufc_athletes.drop_duplicates([...])"
      ],
      "id": "169dde91",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Fill in the code (the `...`), using the columns you chose in the previous question to uniquely identify each athlete.\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:**"
      ],
      "id": "67e9bd80"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "ufc_athletes = ufc_athletes.drop_duplicates(['name', 'weight_class'])"
      ],
      "id": "aa0e6417",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Weight class?\n",
        "\n",
        "We want to `merge` the `ufc_athletes` and the `ufc_fights` datasets together. One column that will help us merge is the `weight_class` column, which appears in each dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "However, we need to check that `weight_class` is recorded in the same way for each table!\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Use [`unique`](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.Series.unique.html) to identify the unique weight classes in the `ufc_athletes` data and the `ufc_fights` data. Do the weight classes agree?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:**"
      ],
      "id": "4c27ba8a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "ufc_athletes['weight_class'].unique()"
      ],
      "id": "e70ee1c4",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: false\n",
        "ufc_fights['weight_class'].unique()"
      ],
      "id": "3f0f5c64",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The weight classes are very different. In the `ufc_athletes` data, we only have the basic weight class (featherweight, bantamweight, etc.), and men vs. women. In the `ufc_fights` data, however, we have a lot of extra information about the actual tournament, which seems unrelated to the actual weight class of the fight.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "### Cleaning weight class\n",
        "\n",
        "To make the weight classes match between the two data frames, we need to clean the entries in the `ufc_fights` data. Carrying out all the necessary cleaning steps is a bit beyond what we have covered in class so far, so I will provide the code here -- but we will discuss some of this material later in the class!\n",
        "\n",
        "The code below converts the weight classes in the `ufc_fights` data into values that match the `ufc_athletes` data, and stores the resulting output in `ufc_fights_clean`."
      ],
      "id": "a4d60fc0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from itertools import chain\n",
        "\n",
        "# unique weight classes from athletes data (converted to string)\n",
        "athlete_weights = ufc_athletes['weight_class'].dropna().unique().astype('U')\n",
        "\n",
        "# separate into an array of key words\n",
        "# (We will keep only key words from this array in the \n",
        "# ufc_fights data)\n",
        "athlete_weights = np.char.split(athlete_weights)\n",
        "weight_keywords = np.unique(list(chain.from_iterable(athlete_weights)))\n",
        "\n",
        "# function to extract just the pieces of weight class that are \n",
        "# in the weight_keywords\n",
        "def filter_words(split_words):\n",
        "  return ' '.join([s for s in split_words if s in weight_keywords])\n",
        "\n",
        "# apply the function to the ufc_fights data\n",
        "ufc_fights_clean = ufc_fights.assign(weight_class = \n",
        "  ufc_fights['weight_class'].str.split(' ').apply(filter_words))"
      ],
      "id": "203556e6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Merging datasets\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Combine the `ufc_fights_clean` dataset and the `ufc_athletes` dataset into a single table that looks like the one below (I am only showing the first few rows), to add information about fighter 1 (`f1_name`).\n",
        "\n",
        "Note:\n",
        "\n",
        "* I have kept only the `weight_class`, `f1_name`, `f2_name`, and `f1_result` columns from `ufc_fights_clean`\n",
        "* I included only the `name`, `weight_class`, `height`, `reach`, and `leg_reach` columns from `ufc_athletes`\n",
        "* If you have duplicate columns after the merge, you can use [`drop`](https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/reference/api/pandas.DataFrame.drop.html)\n"
      ],
      "id": "7d6ff820"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "\n",
        "comb_data = ufc_fights_clean[['weight_class', 'f1_name', 'f2_name', 'f1_result']].merge(ufc_athletes[['name', 'weight_class', 'height', 'reach', 'leg_reach']], how = 'inner', \n",
        "left_on = ['f1_name', 'weight_class'], \n",
        "right_on = ['name', 'weight_class']).drop('name', axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "comb_data.head()"
      ],
      "id": "d036484f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:**"
      ],
      "id": "d5cdb6d7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "comb_data = ufc_fights_clean[['weight_class', 'f1_name', 'f2_name', 'f1_result']].merge(ufc_athletes[['name', 'weight_class', 'height', 'reach', 'leg_reach']], how = 'inner', \n",
        "left_on = ['f1_name', 'weight_class'], \n",
        "right_on = ['name', 'weight_class']).drop('name', axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "comb_data.head()"
      ],
      "id": "40c8d31f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Merge your result from the previous question with the `ufc_athletes` dataset again, this time to add information about fighter 2 (`f2_name`).\n",
        "\n",
        "For this second merge, the `suffixes` argument in the `merge` function may be useful!"
      ],
      "id": "7abcfc59"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "\n",
        "comb_data = comb_data.merge(ufc_athletes[['name', 'weight_class', 'height', 'reach', 'leg_reach']], how = 'inner', \n",
        "left_on = ['f2_name', 'weight_class'], \n",
        "right_on = ['name', 'weight_class'],\n",
        "suffixes = ['_1', '_2'])\n",
        "\n",
        "comb_data.head()"
      ],
      "id": "a79d9915",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:**"
      ],
      "id": "8020c3a7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "comb_data = comb_data.merge(ufc_athletes[['name', 'weight_class', 'height', 'reach', 'leg_reach']], \n",
        "  how = 'inner', left_on = ['f2_name', 'weight_class'], \n",
        "  right_on = ['name', 'weight_class'], suffixes = ['_1', '_2'])\n",
        "\n",
        "comb_data.head()"
      ],
      "id": "5f481cbc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Question\n",
        "\n",
        "Use the `assign` function to create columns for the difference in height, reach, and leg reach between the fighters."
      ],
      "id": "29d2d167"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| include: false\n",
        "\n",
        "comb_data = comb_data.assign(height_diff = comb_data['height_1'] - comb_data['height_2'])"
      ],
      "id": "90a048e9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "**Solution:**"
      ],
      "id": "a902d4db"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "comb_data = comb_data.assign(height_diff = comb_data['height_1'] - comb_data['height_2'])"
      ],
      "id": "f140d07a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Plotting\n",
        "\n",
        "Finally, let's make a plot to examine the relationship between differences in physical characteristics, and the outcome of the fight. One option would be to make some boxplots using `plotly.express`:"
      ],
      "id": "d984c1d6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fig = px.box(comb_data, x=\"f1_result\", y=\"height_diff\")\n",
        "fig.show()"
      ],
      "id": "f6e5029d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
